Subject: [PATCH 11/11] aeraui: build libwebp's SSE2 and SSE4.1 sources

libaera_webp_decoder lists libwebp's NEON sources but not its SSE ones.
On x86 and x86_64, libwebp's dsp.h defines WEBP_HAVE_SSE2 and
WEBP_HAVE_SSE41, so cpu.c's runtime dispatch calls VP8DspInitSSE2,
WebPInitSamplersSSE41 and the other SSE init functions, and recovery
fails to link for an x86_64 target such as Cuttlefish.

List the SSE sources next to the NEON ones, as libwebp's own build does.
Each file is guarded by WEBP_USE_SSE2 or WEBP_USE_SSE41 and compiles to an
empty init stub on ARM, the same way the NEON files do on x86. The
rescaler's SSE2 file stays out: WEBP_REDUCE_SIZE drops its caller.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J6XhHxrkhAcXmkzHMeCnVz
